Here's everything in the **light support** deck, grouped as they're organized in the code:

## Activities (do together)

**Games & puzzles**
- Play a card game
- Play a board game
- Do a jigsaw puzzle
- Crossword or word search
- Quiz each other (trivia)
- Checkers or chess
- Name that tune

**Hands & home**
- Bake something together
- Cook a family recipe
- Tend or repot plants
- Do a simple craft
- Color or paint together
- Make a scrapbook together
- Arrange flowers
- A small task, together
- Fix or tinker with something
- Wrap a gift or prep a card

**Out & about / body**
- Take a walk together
- Sit outside together
- Dance to a favorite song
- Gentle stretches together
- Watch the birds
- A short drive somewhere

**Music & media**
- Listen to music together
- Sing along to old favorites
- Watch a favorite show
- Watch old home videos
- Faith music together
- Flip through a magazine

**Photos & keepsakes**
- Look through photos together
- Go through keepsakes
- Read old letters together
- Reminisce over a map

**Legacy & looking forward** (activities)
- Record them telling a story
- Have them teach you
- Build a life timeline
- Write cards to family

## Talking points (talk cards)

**Legacy & looking forward** (talk)
- Plan something to look forward to
- Catch up, both ways
- Share what you're grateful for

**Ask & listen** (conversation guides from the story bank)
- The house they grew up in
- After-school days
- Brothers and sisters
- Family weekends
- Their first job
- Fun with friends
- Their first car
- A bit of trouble
- How they met their love
- Their kids as little ones
- Who they take after
- A tradition they kept
- The work they did
- What they were great at
- Something they built
- Their hardest job
- A meal they loved
- Music that moves them
- The best place they traveled
- How they unwound
- Something they wish they knew
- What makes a good life
- Advice to their younger self
- How the world has changed

**Totals:** 37 activity cards + 27 talk cards = **64 cards** (24 of the talk cards are the "Ask & listen" question guides).

